  "description": "VOKPAO crystallizes in the trigonal crystal system with space group P -3 c 1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C81 H120 Dy3 N6 Ni3 O22 1+,Cl1 O4 1-,4(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Ni1 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.402-3.818 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.88-108.28°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ni3Dy3(μ3-O)(μ3-OH)3(L)3(μ-OOCCMe3)3](ClO4)·8CH3CN·3CH2Cl2·5.5H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 3 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
